// The tier above the expansion set: what a country that has already built the obvious things
// goes on to build. Every line here is an existing, observable modifier rather than a
// research-only statistic - output, construction, taxes, trade, supply, the army, the fleet -
// and every prerequisite is a technology the game already ships, so nothing here needs a
// second tree to make sense.
//
// Two rules hold, as everywhere in this folder:
//
//   * a `requires` entry must name a technology that exists, or the catalogue reports a
//     broken dependency rather than silently never offering the project;
//   * an `effects` key must be one of the modifier keys the simulation actually reads
//     (see Scripts/Simulation/NationalModifiers.cs). A typo is an error with the list
//     beside it, not a bonus that quietly does nothing.
